# Key Insights
 
## Customer Retention
 
The company retains approximately 73% of customers, while 26.54% of customers have churned.
 
## Contract Analysis
 
Month-to-month customers exhibit significantly higher churn compared to one-year and two-year contract customers.
 
## Customer Tenure
 
Customers who churn have a substantially shorter average tenure than retained customers.
 
## Monthly Charges
 
Customers who churn tend to have higher average monthly charges than retained customers.
 
## Internet Services
 
Fiber optic customers appear more likely to churn than customers using other internet service options.
 
## Payment Methods
 
Customers using electronic checks show higher churn levels than customers using other payment methods.
 
## Recommendations
 
1. Encourage customers to move from month-to-month contracts to longer-term contracts.
2. Improve onboarding and engagement for new customers.
3. Review pricing strategies for higher-risk customer segments.
4. Investigate reasons for churn among fiber optic customers.
5. Develop targeted retention campaigns for electronic check users.
